+
+### Mermaid in terminal previews
+
+The listed preview (`require('render-markdown').preview()`) renders complete
+`mermaid` fenced blocks with `mermaid-ascii`. Install that executable on PATH,
+or configure its location before opening a preview:
+
+```lua
+require('render-markdown.core.preview').mermaid = {
+    command = '/path/to/mermaid-ascii',
+    timeout = 5000, -- milliseconds
+}
+```
+
+The converter receives source on stdin (`mermaid-ascii -f -`) with `NO_COLOR=1`.
+Conversion runs asynchronously. Diagrams keep their spaces and line boundaries;
+wide diagrams scroll horizontally instead of wrapping. Source files are never
+changed. Other fenced code remains literal. Only Mermaid syntax supported by
+your installed converter renders; failed, empty, timed-out, or unavailable
+conversion leaves the original fence in the preview and reports a warning.
+Unchanged failed inputs are cached, avoiding repeated warnings during refresh.
+Close and reopen to retry after installing or repairing the converter.
+
+Each open preview owns a ten-entry conversion cache; repeated identical
+blocks share a process. Refresh ignores results for superseded source revisions,
+and closing the preview cancels pending work.
